7) Analytics (where to fire)

guardian_link_attempt {method}: on “Lookup” (code) & on “Scan” (qr)

guardian_link_success {method}: on createLink success → active

guardian_link_failure {reason}: on API error (code from server)

link_pending_wait_ms: when PendingApproval resolves

8) QA checklist (M1)

Valid code → preview → confirm → active → Success screen.

Valid code → pending → Pending screen → after admin flip → auto routes to Success.

Invalid/expired/max-uses → correct localized error.

5 failed codes/15min → TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS message.

QR with tuto://link?code=… or plain code → same flow.

Cancel from Pending → link revoked; trying to poll returns terminal state.

9) Notes / small gotchas

For now, QR tab just parses a code from QR; when you add /api/students/getByQrToken, switch parseQrPayloadToCode to hit that endpoint and then call createLink(..., 'qr').

On success, if the server can return studentId with the link, navigate directly to children/[childId]/consents/index when required consents are pending.